      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Strong arguments often draw from libertarian political philosophy, emphasizing individual liberty and the right to unhindered expression against state overreach. You can lean on the First Amendment's strong defense of the \"marketplace of ideas,\" suggesting that any regulation inherently limits the discourse necessary for truth to emerge.\n\nAdditionally, some arguments from absolute libertarianism claim that the state's power to regulate opinion is inherently coercive and an attack on personal sovereignty, framing all restrictions as ideological censorship.\n\nI recommend further exploring the anti-paternalism arguments, which assert that the government should not \"think for\" the user regarding acceptable online speech.",
